## Rules when the brain is unavailable

- Read `CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code) or `AGENTS.md` (other agents) first.
- The canonical brain remains the home for implementation plans and handoffs. Do not
  create standalone plan mirrors in the repo.
- If you must record something while the brain is down, add a dated note to this file
  only, tell the user the brain was unavailable, and sync it into the brain as soon as
  the backend is back.
- Never work around a permission failure by writing somewhere else. If a write to the
  intended destination is refused, stop and report it.
